       "reasons": [
        {
         "@type": "meaningComprehension",
         "comprehends": [
          "copies/nq190zp1066.jsonld#inscription-text"
         ],
         "note": "Faint pencil, six figures in three pairs with the separators dropped: 21.12.21. The same line appears on crop 1, and on both it sits within a few millimetres of the crop's edge, so the upper halves of the figures lie in the shadow of the boundary; the reading is sure of the pairing and of the repeated 2 and 1 shapes, less sure of any single figure, hence medium. Crop 6 carries 1341 on its own, which I take for the roll number. Crop 3 shows one clipped mark, crop 4 a row of small pencil loops drawn round particular perforations, which look like a repairer's or inspector's marks rather than writing, and crop 5 the paper end."
        }
       ]
      }
     }
    },
